Z||000013||SloPonti||01-08-2001||12:31 AM||||here is my hopped up iron duck! it features a comp cam-holley throttle body-hooker tri-y header-msd blaster coil-high volume oil pump-port and polish-three angle valve job-accell 8mm wires-true ram air setup from side scoop to intake-K&N filter-hypertechtic pistions with chrome molley rings-bored .40 over! check out the pitures!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/fiero4.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by SloPonti (edited 01-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||jerpro||01-08-2001||01:51 PM||||WOw man!!! I almost forgot to breathe while reading all you did to your fiero!! <BR>How exactly dod you do the true ram air install?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||SloPonti||01-09-2001||12:33 AM||||i got the holley replica side scoop and put it on plus i got rid of the stock airbox inside the inner drivers side rear wheel well and made my own 3 inch pvc pipe to go into its place then added more tubing from there to the air cleaner housing! so there is a direct flow from the side scoop to the throttle body with no restrictions except the k&n filter!||||reg||1
